'' =================================================================================================
''
''   File....... isp_bench_commit.spin2
''   Purpose.... The commit a bench binary was built from, printed in every bench harness banner
''   Authors.... Stephen M Moraco
''               -- Copyright (c) 2026 Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''               -- see below for terms of use
''   E-mail..... stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started.... 01 Oct 2026
''   Updated.... 01 Oct 2026
''
'' =================================================================================================
''
''  THIS TRACKED COPY IS NEVER EDITED. It reads "not a pack": a binary compiled from the source tree
''  prints NOT_A_PACK, since that tree may hold uncommitted changes. tools/make-bench-pack.sh compiles
''  inside a git-archive copy of a commit, and writes that copy's version of this file (the commit's
''  short SHA, and COMMIT_PACKED TRUE) before compiling, echoing what it writes. So a bench log names
''  the exact commit only when it came from a pack.
''

CON { the build's commit }

    COMMIT_PACKED = FALSE                                       ' TRUE only in a pack's own copy of this file

DAT { the commit, as printed }

    sCommit     BYTE    "NOT_A_PACK", 0                         ' a pack writes its commit's short SHA here

PUB commitText() : pText
'' Return the build's commit as text: the short SHA in a pack, NOT_A_PACK from the source tree.
''
'' @returns pText - pointer to the zero-terminated commit text

    pText := @sCommit

CON { license }

